  "id": "double-aspect-theory",
  "term": "double-aspect theory",
  "definition": "Double-aspect theory is a historical view of the mind-body relation holding that mental events and bodily events are parallel expressions of one underlying reality. It treats conscious and physical processes as different but not reducible to each other, and denies that mind and body directly cause one another.",
